# Test: `system conntrack module ftp` installs the ftp ct helper and assigns it.
# VALIDATES: spec-home-cpe-3 AC-1 -- a config with no firewall {} block
#            starts the firewall engine on its system/conntrack root, which
#            lowers the listed helper (ConntrackHelperTables), the nft
#            backend installs the inet table ze_conntrack_helpers, and
#            `nft list table` shows the ct helper object ftp-tcp (kernel
#            helper "ftp", protocol tcp) and a rule assigning it to tcp 21 in
#            both the prerouting and the output chain at priority filter - 5.
# PREVENTS: a listed helper that is accepted and assigns nothing (the state
#           before this spec: modprobe only, a no-op on Ze's kernel, and no
#           kernel since 6.0 assigns a helper without an explicit rule).
#
# Requires CAP_NET_ADMIN and a kernel that provides nf_conntrack_ftp (built in
# on Ze's kernel). The fixture waits up to 15 s (registerTableSnapshot), under
# the 20 s timeout. Without the helper the kernel refuses the ct helper object,
# the table is never created, and the fixture's `nft list table` fails.

# The conntrack-helper-* tests all program the one inet ze_conntrack_helpers
# table in the node-wide ruleset, and each removes it again (a reload that
# drops the module, or flush-on-shutdown when the fixture stops the daemon).
# Run together, one deletes the table a sibling is still asserting on, so the
# group keeps them apart (TestContendingFunctionalTestsDeclareExclusiveGroup).

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin
option=exclusive:group=conntrack-helpers

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	conntrack {
		module ftp;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture firewall/conntrack-helper-ftp-assigned:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=table inet ze_conntrack_helpers
expect=stdout:pattern=ct helper "?ftp-tcp"? \{
expect=stdout:pattern=type "ftp" protocol tcp
expect=stdout:pattern=hook prerouting priority (filter - 5|-5)
expect=stdout:pattern=hook output priority (filter - 5|-5)
# ze places an anonymous counter at the term's match/action boundary
# (withCounter, internal/plugins/firewall/nft/lower_linux.go).
expect=stdout:pattern=(tcp|th) dport 21 counter packets [0-9]+ bytes [0-9]+ ct helper set "ftp-tcp"
